# Security checklist

When changing auth, APIs, payments, AI tools, DB, or deploy config, verify the relevant items below. Prefer fixing in the same PR over deferring.

## Secrets & config
1. No DB credentials, API keys, or tokens in source, commits, or client bundles
2. Never commit `.env`; only placeholders in `.env.example`
3. No hardcoded secrets; fail closed in production if required keys are missing (`AGNTPYMT_MCP_KEY`, Clerk, etc.)
4. No secrets in frontend (`VITE_*` is public) or production source maps
5. No secrets in build logs, health endpoints, or error responses

## Auth & sessions
6. Authentication required on all non-public routes; no silent “auth off → org_demo” in production
7. Strong session/JWT handling; no tokens in query strings (`__clerk_token`)
8. Cookies: HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite when cookies are used
9. No default/dev credentials in production (`dev-mcp-key`, `agntpymt/agntpymt`)
10. Password reset / Clerk flows must not leak account existence or tokens

## Authorization & tenancy
11. Every data access scoped by `orgId` (and agent ownership where applicable)
12. No IDOR: never trust client-supplied IDs/roles without ownership checks
13. Admin / seller / MCP routes enforced server-side — never `VITE_*` alone
14. MCP and AI tools must not read/write other orgs’ data or dump unscoped tables
15. Payment/spend authorization only on the server (policy, caps, kill switch)

## Injection & request safety
16. Validate/sanitize all inputs (Zod); parameterized queries only (Drizzle/`eq`)
17. No XSS (`dangerouslySetInnerHTML` without sanitization); escape AI/chat output
18. CSRF: prefer Bearer auth; if cookies, use SameSite + CSRF tokens
19. No path traversal on skill/profile/file paths (`..`, unsanitized IDs)
20. No SSRF / arbitrary `command`/`url` from users into Hermes/MCP without allowlists
21. No insecure file uploads; webhook endpoints need signature verification

## Network & abuse
22. CORS allowlist — never `origin: true` in production
23. Rate-limit login, signup, AI, purchase, and MCP endpoints
24. Security headers (Helmet/CSP/HSTS) on the API and static UI
25. Do not expose debug pages, internal dashboards, or verbose stack traces in production

## Payments & wallets
26. Never return or log wallet private keys; encrypt/KMS at rest — plaintext DB keys are forbidden for production
27. Live payment mode requires auth + verified payee config; simulation must be explicit
28. Frontend payment UI is display-only; settlement and policy checks are backend

## AI-specific
29. Treat user/agent text as untrusted (prompt injection); keep pricing/policy in code
30. AI tools/actions require the same org/agent permission checks as human APIs

## Ops & supply chain
31. Least-privilege DB user; do not publish Postgres to the public internet
32. Audit logs for approvals, spends, policy changes; monitoring/alerting for auth and payment failures
33. Keep dependencies updated; review generated code before shipping
34. Backups/restore plan for Postgres and profile storage

## AgntPymt known hotspots (check these first)
- Public path bypass: `server/src/middleware/auth.ts` (`/agent/execute`)
- MCP key default: `server/src/config.ts` (`dev-mcp-key`)
- Run history/SSE org checks: `server/src/routes/api.ts`
- CORS: `server/src/index.ts`
- Wallet key storage: `server/src/services/agent-wallet.ts`
- Hermes MCP `command`/`url` upserts and skill path IDs: `hermes-profile.ts`
